# Code owners for OpenTag. See CONTRIBUTING.md, section "Code ownership".
#
# Last matching pattern wins. Each pattern also carries a mode (gate / territory
# / exempt) declared in .github/ownership-modes.json and enforced by the
# ownership-gate required status check; a pattern with no mode entry there is
# treated as gate. Gate is the DEFAULT: anything new, anywhere, is mutually
# reviewed until a reviewed edit of these two files relaxes it (fail-safe all
# the way down).
#
# Ownership is derived from change history and recalculated monthly.
# baixiaohang is on leave; bestony holds that territory until the recalculation.

# Gate by default: mutual review, no author self-exemption.
*                           @bestony @yuezengwu

# Territory carve-outs: routine chores, owner-author self-merges on green CI.
/pnpm-lock.yaml             @bestony @yuezengwu
/.editorconfig              @bestony @yuezengwu
/.gitignore                 @bestony @yuezengwu
/LICENSE                    @bestony @yuezengwu

# Docs fast lane: territory. Overrides the gate for markdown anywhere outside web.
*.md                        @yuezengwu @bestony @Gandy2025 @liuchao-001

# Gate pins. Both sit BELOW *.md because the markdown fast lane would otherwise
# win for the one markdown file each of them contains, and a pin that a later
# rule overrides protects nothing. check-ownership-policy.mjs fails the build if
# a later rule ever wins for a file beneath either pattern.
#
# .github holds the ownership gate itself, the CI workflows that decide what
# "green CI" means, and the pull request template. It must not be reachable
# through the documentation fast lane.
/.github/                   @bestony @yuezengwu

# Irreversible migrations and the CURRENT_MIGRATION_COUNT ratchet stay gated
# even if a broader rule is ever relaxed.
/packages/server/drizzle/   @bestony @yuezengwu

# Gate carve-back: root policy / agent-instruction files are behavior, not docs
# (AGENTS/CLAUDE steer the agents working in this repo; CONTRIBUTING documents
# this policy itself; SECURITY is the disclosure policy).
# zh-CN mirrors move with their canonical documents.
/AGENTS.md                  @yuezengwu @bestony
/CLAUDE.md                  @yuezengwu @bestony
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @yuezengwu @bestony
/CONTRIBUTING.zh-CN.md      @yuezengwu @bestony
/SECURITY.md                @yuezengwu @bestony
/SECURITY.zh-CN.md          @yuezengwu @bestony

# Exempt: no owners on purpose. Placed last so it carves web out of the gate and
# also overrides *.md inside web: nothing under apps/web requires code-owner
# approval or auto-requests reviewers.
/apps/web/
